## Project

Web app that converts uploaded images into cross-stitch embroidery patterns.
Currently a frontend-only MVP — the pattern generation logic is not yet implemented.

**Stack:** React Router 7 (SSR), React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS 4, i18next (EN/RU), vite-plugin-pwa, react-dropzone, Sonner.

## Architecture

- `app/components/` — shared, reusable UI components
- `app/pages/` — page-level components (`welcome/`, `preview/`)
- `app/routes/` — React Router route handlers; keep thin, delegate to pages
- `app/contexts/` — React Context providers (currently only `ThemeContext`)
- `app/hooks/` — custom hooks
- `app/i18n/` — i18next config + all EN/RU translation strings in `resources.ts`
- `app/utils/` — pure utility functions

Larger components live in their own folder with subcomponents inside a `components/` subfolder (see `FileDropzone/` as the reference example).

## Code conventions

- TypeScript everywhere, no `any`
- Functional components only, no class components
- Props interfaces defined inline or just above the component
- Tailwind for all styling — no separate CSS files except `app/app.css` for global theme variables
- Dark mode via `dark:` Tailwind prefix; primary brand color is `#6b449a` (purple)

## i18n

Every user-visible string must go through i18next — no hardcoded UI text.
All translation keys live in `app/i18n/resources.ts`. Add both `en` and `ru` translations whenever you add a new key.

Usage in components:
```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation();
// ...
<p>{t('some.key')}</p>
```

## Theme

Theme state lives in `ThemeContext`. Use the `useTheme` hook to read or toggle it — do not read `localStorage` directly in components.

## SSR considerations

This app uses server-side rendering. Avoid direct `window`/`document` access at the module level. Use `useIsomorphicLayoutEffect` instead of `useLayoutEffect` where needed.

